 "props": {
  "doc": "Pieces of x08 \"Just Let Me Pay\" (scripts/x08-art-gen.py, scripts/x08-prep.py); this text is props.doc. Puppets (ross, rossPeel) are cut like tip-rig.json's, in px of the picture PADDED by `pad` on every side (1024 + 2 pad square, y down); pivot = the neck. ross: ONE head (the master's, ross-sit-61) and a body per pose (sit, up, fly: the pose pictures registered on the head, which is why the standing ones are 1.45 and 1.65 times bigger than they were painted); plugs = the two ear tunnels [cx, cy, r], the picture's left one first; headFiles = the head with the left plug gone (l), both gone (none): the lobe is a ring with a hole through it; red = the 'none' head with the skin turned red; flySil = a white silhouette of the flying Ross from his raised hands to his belly, and the same shape filled with a sky (file, sky, w, h, pivot). screens.sit / screens.up = the glass of the phone in that body picture: file (a mask of the body layer's size), cx, cy, w, h, turn (px of the layer, turn clockwise in degrees). rossPeel: the peel picture (both hands on his cheeks), its own head, one body. props.hand = the hand with the phone for the inserts (file, screenFile = the glass as a mask of the same size, screen = [x0, y0, x1, y1] of the glass in the layer's px, ox, oy = the layer's place in the 1024 picture, skin, ink). scenes.living = the plate x08-bg-living.jpg (768 x 1344): ceiling = the row where the ceiling band ends, window = the frame's box, panes = the three panes of its glass, backTop = the couch back's top, seatTop and seatFront = the cushion's top and its front edge, floor = where the couch stands, wallFloor = where the wall meets the floor, lamp = the lamp shade's box.",
